The '''Tesla Model 3''' is a [[Battery electric vehicle|battery electric]] powered <!-- Tesla does not call the Model 3 a luxury or executive car. -->[[Mid-size car|mid-size sedan]] with a [[fastback]] body style built by [[Tesla, Inc.]], introduced in 2017. The vehicle is marketed as being more affordable to more people than previous models made by Tesla. The Model 3 was the world's top-selling [[plug-in electric car]] for three years, from 2018 to 2020,<!-- <ref name="Top20Global2020" /><ref name="Top20Global2018" /><ref name="Top20Global2019" /> --> before the [[Tesla Model Y]], a crossover [[SUV]] based on the Model 3 chassis, took the top spot. In June 2021, the Model 3 became the first electric car to pass global sales of 1&nbsp;million.

A [[facelift (automotive)|facelifted]] Model 3 with revamped interior and exterior styling was introduced in late 2023 for countries supplied by [[Gigafactory Shanghai]] and in early 2024 in North America and other countries supplied by the [[Tesla Fremont Factory]].

